<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rhenish Hesse</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Rheinhessen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rhenish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> is a region on the left bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> and Worms, known for its vineyards. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> settlement gave it to the Grand Duchy of Hesse in 1816 in exchange for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a>, and it remained one of Hesse's three provinces until 1945. It then became part of the new state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland-palatinate">Rhineland-Palatinate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rhenish-hesse.jpg" alt="Rhenish Hesse" width="176" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dexx · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rheinhessen.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
